      "id": "java-se-standard-edition",
      "heading": "Java SE (Standard Edition)",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Java SE is essentially the Java Development Kit (JDK).",
            "It includes: ",
            "Java Virtual Machine (JVM): Executes Java applications using JRE libraries.",
            "📝 Note: From JDK 11 onwards, JRE is no longer a separate component."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 34,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "how-java-works",
          "heading": "How Java Works",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "JDK: Everything needed to write and compile Java code.",
                "JRE: Resources required to run Java applications.",
                "JVM: Executes the Java code in a platform-independent virtual environment."
              ]
            },
